{"name":"Daystar","hex":"#fff8da","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"daystar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The planet Venus as the morning star.","The Sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daystar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"},{"title":"Daystar (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Daystar is the fifth studio album by Canadian singer and rapper Tory Lanez. It was released on September 25, 2020, by One Umbrella Records and was his first independent release after departing from Interscope Records. The music was largely written by Lanez and produced with a variety of record producers, while featuring a sole guest appearance by fellow rapper Yoko Gold."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Tory_Lanez_-_Daystar.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daystar_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/500px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/1280px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm